1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,877
How many kilos of feed does one kilo of beef buy?

2
00:00:03,877 --> 00:00:05,277
In America in 1974:

3
00:00:05,277 --> 00:00:06,677
half a kilo.

4
00:00:06,677 --> 00:00:08,077
Today:

5
00:00:08,077 --> 00:00:09,477
more than two.

6
00:00:09,477 --> 00:00:12,954
Everything between those two numbers is one pattern.

7
00:00:12,954 --> 00:00:13,020
And it is repeating right now.

8
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:15,393
The mechanism never changes.

9
00:00:15,393 --> 00:00:16,793
Feed gets expensive.

10
00:00:16,793 --> 00:00:18,193
Herds get slaughtered.

11
00:00:18,193 --> 00:00:21,020
And three years later, there is not enough beef.

12
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:23,120
Nineteen seventy-two.

13
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:28,670
The Soviet Union hides a failed harvest and quietly buys a quarter of the American wheat crop.

14
00:00:28,670 --> 00:00:30,070
Then the oil embargo.

15
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:31,470
Corn tripled.

16
00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:34,250
And this line fell to the lowest point it has ever reached.

17
00:00:34,950 --> 00:00:36,350
Two thousand twelve.

18
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:37,750
The Great Plains burned.

19
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:40,810
Feed got expensive, so ranchers slaughtered the herd.

20
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:42,773
Three years later beef was scarce,

21
00:00:42,773 --> 00:00:44,380
and the parity hit a record.

22
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:46,631
Nineteen seventy-four.

23
00:00:46,631 --> 00:00:48,031
Ninety-six.

24
00:00:48,031 --> 00:00:49,441
Two thousand eleven.

25
00:00:49,441 --> 00:00:50,841
Twenty twenty-one.

26
00:00:50,841 --> 00:00:53,239
Four different decades, one curve.

27
00:00:53,239 --> 00:00:56,976
Three to four times higher, in forty to fifty months.

28
00:00:56,976 --> 00:00:57,740
Every single time.

29
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:01,625
Turkiye joins the screen in 2010, Europe in 2015.

30
00:01:01,625 --> 00:01:03,025
This is not a race.

31
00:01:03,025 --> 00:01:06,210
Each country is measured against its own average.

32
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:07,965
And where is America today?

33
00:01:07,965 --> 00:01:10,175
Eighty-four percent above its own.

34
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:14,667
Twenty twenty-one was the first time the wave hit everyone at once.

35
00:01:14,667 --> 00:01:16,161
But not at the same moment.

36
00:01:16,161 --> 00:01:17,711
America bottomed out in May.

37
00:01:17,711 --> 00:01:19,111
Turkiye six months later,

38
00:01:19,111 --> 00:01:20,826
and the currency made it worse.

39
00:01:20,826 --> 00:01:22,265
Europe a full year behind.

40
00:01:22,265 --> 00:01:23,665
Same wave.

41
00:01:23,665 --> 00:01:24,490
Three different landfalls.

42
00:01:25,190 --> 00:01:26,853
So what does the feeder earn?

43
00:01:26,853 --> 00:01:29,031
Hold the calf and the overheads fixed,

44
00:01:29,031 --> 00:01:30,431
and only feed moves.

45
00:01:30,431 --> 00:01:32,782
On that basis, all three are green today.

46
00:01:32,782 --> 00:01:35,420
But in America the calf itself is at a record.

47
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:38,286
The real margin is thinner than this chart admits.

48
00:01:38,286 --> 00:01:40,064
Parity gives you the direction.

49
00:01:40,064 --> 00:01:41,150
Not the whole bill.

50
00:01:41,850 --> 00:01:43,775
The wave is the same everywhere.

51
00:01:43,775 --> 00:01:45,175
The shield is not.

52
00:01:45,175 --> 00:01:47,642
America locks the margin on the exchange.

53
00:01:47,642 --> 00:01:49,869
Europe cashes a cheque from Brussels.

54
00:01:49,869 --> 00:01:52,335
The Turkish feeder has no futures market.

55
00:01:52,335 --> 00:01:53,735
No margin insurance.

56
00:01:53,735 --> 00:01:55,420
And credit at fifty percent.

57
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:56,360
Same wave.

58
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:56,360
No shield.

59
00:01:57,060 --> 00:01:58,460
So where are we now?

60
00:01:58,460 --> 00:01:59,860
At the top.

61
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:03,718
The highest parity America has seen in fifty-five years.

62
00:02:03,718 --> 00:02:06,405
Every previous peak ended the same way:

63
00:02:06,405 --> 00:02:09,918
herds rebuild, supply returns, and the ratio falls.

64
00:02:09,918 --> 00:02:11,778
It has happened four times.

65
00:02:11,778 --> 00:02:13,178
This is the fifth.

66
00:02:13,178 --> 00:02:15,039
You cannot shrink the wave.

67
00:02:15,039 --> 00:02:15,980
You can only price it.
